      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 1999 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "We report a technique for retrieval of a dislodged coronary stent using a stiff angioplasty wire positioned beside the initial stent guidewire. This two-wire technique provides a better platform to move and position the snare device without moving the dislodged stent and thus lessens the risk of embolization. If a larger femoral sheath is needed for stent removal, this method facilitates sheath exchange. Cathet. Cardiovasc. Intervent. 47:323-324, 1999."
      },
